"`plot_layout` returns `None`. With `formats=\"all\"`, it writes PDF, PNG, "
"and SVG files. A higher-dimensional `T.Layout` is flattened to a two-"
"dimensional grid: all dimensions except the last form the row coordinate, "
"and the last dimension forms the column coordinate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/layout_visualization.md:85
msgid "Visualize Inferred Layouts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/layout_visualization.md:87
msgid "Enable the compiler pass through `pass_configs` on a JIT kernel:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/layout_visualization.md:89
msgid ""
"import tilelang\n"
"import tilelang.language as T\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"@tilelang.jit(\n"
"    pass_configs={\n"
"        tilelang.PassConfigKey.TL_LAYOUT_VISUALIZATION_ENABLE: True,\n"
"        tilelang.PassConfigKey.TL_LAYOUT_VISUALIZATION_FORMATS: \"txt,"
"svg\",\n"
"    }\n"
")\n"
"def kernel(A, block_M, block_N):\n"
"    M, N = T.const(\"M, N\")\n"
"    A: T.Tensor((M, N), T.float16)\n"
"    B = T.empty((M, N), T.float16)\n"
"\n"
"    with T.Kernel(T.ceildiv(N, block_N), T.ceildiv(M, block_M), threads=128) "
"as (bx, by):\n"
"        fragment = T.alloc_fragment((block_M, block_N), T.float16)\n"
"        T.copy(A[by * block_M, bx * block_N], fragment)\n"
"        T.copy(fragment, B[by * block_M, bx * block_N])\n"
"\n"
"    return B\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/layout_visualization.md:113
msgid ""
"Compile or invoke the kernel normally. For each inferred `T.Fragment` found "
"in a block's `layout_map` annotation, the pass prints output like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/layout_visualization.md:116
msgid ""
"C_local inferred layout:\n"
"  Shape: [32, 32] -> [8]\n"
"  Thread: <thread-index expression>\n"
"  Index:  [<local-index expression>]\n"
"  Replicate:  1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/layout_visualization.md:124
msgid ""
"Image files are written under `./tmp` with names derived from the buffer, "
"such as `C_local_layout.svg`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/layout_visualization.md:127
msgid ""
"`TL_LAYOUT_VISUALIZATION_ENABLE` defaults to `False`. When it is enabled, "
"`TL_LAYOUT_VISUALIZATION_FORMATS` accepts `txt`, `png`, `pdf`, `svg`, `all`, "
"or a comma-separated combination. Omitting the formats setting selects text-"
"only output. The compiler prints the textual mapping whenever visualization "
"is enabled; `txt` does not add an image format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/layout_visualization.md:133
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/layout_visualization.md:135
msgid ""
"Direct `T.Fragment` plotting requires a two-dimensional input shape and "
"single-valued thread and local-index mappings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/layout_visualization.md:137
msgid ""
"Compiler-generated images are limited to inferred fragments with two-"
"dimensional input shapes. Other inferred fragment shapes are still printed, "
"but image generation is skipped with a warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/layout_visualization.md:140
msgid ""
"Plots enumerate layout elements in Python. Large shapes can produce large "
"figures and take substantial time and memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/layout_visualization.md:142
msgid ""
"The output-space view infers its shape from mapped coordinates. Mappings "
"that are non-bijective or sparse may overwrite a cell or leave empty cells, "
"so the plot should be treated as a diagnostic view rather than layout "
"validation."
msgstr ""

